  "installNotes": [
   "Outdoor installation only. Approx. weight 223 kg (490 lb) with aluminum enclosure; ships on an aluminum skid. Lift with bars through the skid holes (TP-6925 p.12).",
   "Set on gravel with weed barrier or a concrete pad - never on grass or wood. High-wind sites (up to 181 mph): concrete pad and four mounting bolts per the dimension drawing (TP-6925 p.12).",
   "No plants or combustibles within 1.2 m (4 ft) of the exhaust end (TP-6925 p.12; TP-6926 p.57). TP-6805 p.28 says 2.4 m (8 ft) - use the larger. Exhaust air about 260 C (500 F) leaving the enclosure.",
   "Gas pipe size from the primary regulator (add 2.4 m / 8 ft per 90 deg elbow), in. NPT, NG / LP: 8 m (25 ft) 1 / 3/4; 15 m (50 ft) 1 / 1; 30 m (100 ft) 1 1/4 / 1; 46-61 m (150-200 ft) 1 1/4 / 1 1/4 (TP-6925 p.14). Note TP-6803 lists 3/4 in. NG for 25 ft on the 20RESA/C - the 20RESB/D table says 1 in. Fuel inlet 1/2 in. NPT; flexible section at the set.",
   "Hold the fuel solenoid valve on its body flats with a wrench when tightening - never the coil (TP-6925 p.15).",
   "Ground to the equipment ground terminal; breaker on AC circuits max 125% of rated current. 120 VAC from the load side of the ATS to the terminal block for the charger and heaters.",
   "RXT: A, B, PWR, COM from TB2 to RXT P10 (shielded twisted pair, shield grounded at generator only, separate conduit). Other ATS: engine start leads to 3 and 4. Do not use a Model RRT. De-energize the RDC2 before RBUS wiring (SB-813).",
   "Battery: group 26, 500 CCA; install fully charged, positive first then negative.",
   "SB-749 (20RESB with CH1000): pre-lube at startup - remove oil pressure switch, add about 2 oz oil, reinstall at 10.7 Nm (95 in-lb) with PST 592, crank 3 cycles with fuel off, clear overcrank, start and run 1 min before loading.",
   "SB-751: 20RESB built 1/1/2015-7/9/2015 - replace field terminal blocks GND/L0/load before operating (kit GM98599-KP for 2-pole single-phase).",
   "Thermostat: resettable thermostat in the air intake compartment shuts the set down on enclosure overheat (shows as underspeed, underfrequency or undervoltage) - see TP-6944.",
   "Cold weather (below 0 C / 32 F): carburetor heater and breather tube/oil heater kits; fuel regulator heater below -18 C (0 F). 120 VAC heater power must be backed up by the generator.",
   "Paralleling: two 20RESA/B/C/D sets with the same voltage via the PowerSync APM (RDC2 paralleling firmware 105.4+)."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Original controllers (to 2014): green circuit board, USB port and mini-breaker behind a thumbscrew cover. Revised controllers: red board, USB under a small rubber cover, aux winding mini-breaker mounted near (not on) the controller. Replacing green with red needs kit GM95104 (run relay, fuse P22, adapter harness, mini-breaker). Do not load settings from a green-board controller onto a red-board one or vice versa (TP-6805 p.37, p.52-56).",
   "After any controller replacement: update firmware, set genset model, serial, fuel type (firmware 4.5+), system voltage/frequency/phase, calibrate voltage, reset the OnCue password and confirm OnCue Plus connects before leaving.",
   "SiteTech calibration: new factor = (meter volts / controller volts) x old factor. Example 241.2 / 240 x 1.0063 = 1.0113. On RDC2 you can also calibrate from Generator Metering with the arrow keys.",
   "Engine speed: RPM = (system Hz x 60) + ((Engine Speed Adjustment - 50) x 2). Leave it at 50 after testing. Speed gain default 50 (35-65): slow hunting (more than 1 s per swing) = raise gain; fast hunting = lower gain; change in steps of 5 or less.",
   "Firmware milestones from the manuals: 4.03+ for load management, 4.09+ for hunting fix, 4.5+ adds Fuel Type, 5.04+ Advanced Diagnostic and RDT load shed, 5.07+ for OnCue Plus, 5.5+ for E-stop, 6.1+ languages, 6.7+ stops nuisance MainPwrOverL. Version 4.03 = 4.3; SiteTech may show a third digit.",
   "Default crank cycle 15 s on / 15 s rest, 3 cycles (adjustable 10-30 s, 1-60 s, 1-6 cycles); crank disconnect 750 rpm; cooldown 300 s (5 min). Smart cooldown stops early when the engine is cool - set any non-RXT ATS cooldown to zero/minimum.",
   "Start sequence: start signal energizes FP (field flash) and lead 71 (start relay). Once alternator voltage/frequency is seen, lead 70 (run relay on units built 8/1/2014 or later) feeds the fuel valve and ignition, the stepper opens the throttle, and lead 71 drops at 750 rpm (12.5 Hz). Units built before 8/1/2014 have only a start relay under the controller.",
   "Relay pinout (TP-6805 p.123): start relay 30=14P, 85=N7, 86=71, 87=14S; run relay 30=P1, 85=N5, 86=70, 87=70C.",
   "Megger stator and rotor at 500 VDC: about 500 kOhm or more is good; lower means insulation breakdown. Most ohmmeters are not accurate below 1 ohm - for the stator, continuity and no discoloration is a pass.",
   "Event log: RDC2 keeps up to 1000 events (W/S/I with engine hours); DC2 keeps 10 - press OFF, then hold OFF to view, AUTO to exit.",
   "Loaded exercise (RXT only) drops building power for up to 10 s at each transfer - warn the customer.",
   "OnCue password reset: RDC2 - Networking Information > Networking Configuration > hold Select at Reset OnCue Password, Up for Yes, Select; new password shows for 10 s. DC2 - in OFF, hold EXERCISE until \"Press Again to Reset OnCue PW\", press again within 5 s.",
   "SB-752: RDC2/DC2 built before 9/15/2014 (green board; build date on the back label) benefit from battery charging diode harness kit GM95500 (TT-1647), free of charge, install at routine service.",
   "SB-743: stuck rotor - make a jacking tool from a rotor thrubolt (GM76192 or GM62982, 7/16-14) cut to 29.2 cm (11 1/2 in.) with a slot, and a 1/2-20 UNF grade 8 jacking bolt about 7.6 cm (3 in.) long; soak the crank nose with penetrating oil. Never strike the slip rings.",
   "SB-805 / PB-169: 20 kW CH1000 standard oil filter 52 050 02-S (yellow); from 2/25/2022 to about mid-2022 the 14 kW filter 12 050 01-S (black) was used as a substitute on 20 kW engines. Same change procedure. 20 kW maintenance kits GM62347 / GM62347-SKP1-QS.",
   "SB-787: breather tube heaters cut breather tube life - replace with service kit GM108014-S1 (120 V kits) or GM108014-S2 (240 V kits) per the SB table, with new breather tube (TT-1773). No 240 V service kit - use the 120 V one.",
   "SB-731 / TP-6803: hold the fuel solenoid valve on its body flats with a 1 7/8 in. wrench when tightening the gas connection - never by the coil (not covered by warranty).",
   "Do not set the exerciser twice: with a non-RXT ATS, an exercise at the ATS overlapping the generator exercise takes priority.",
   "20RESB has an oil cooler (clean yearly or 150 h); TP-6926 marks it 20RESB only. G4-247 lists the 20RESD oil cooler as \"integral\".",
   "20RESB/RESD were documented with RDC2 only - no DC2 versions in these manuals.",
   "Thermostat reset (TP-6944): utility power off, roof open on its stay, remove the right-side service door (plug + two screws) and front panel (four screws), battery negative off, press the thermostat button, reassemble, restore power, reset the fault. TP-6805 p.66 says to remove the air intake end panel on 20RESB/D."
  ],
