  "specs": {
   "oil": "Synthetic multi-viscosity SAE 5W-30, API SJ or higher, with the API Starburst 'for gasoline engines' mark. 10W-30 synthetic only where temps are never or rarely below 0°C (32°F). Do not use straight-weight or CC/CD 'natural gas engine' oils. Kohler Genuine 5W-30 synthetic: GM103159 (case of 12 qt) (TP-6904 p.11).",
   "oilCapacity": "4.2 L (4.4 qt) all six models (TP-6907 p.25, TP-6905 p.65; engine dry fill 4.2 L per TP-6901 p.61). Spec sheets: oil added at a normal oil change about 3.3 L (3.5 qt). Fill, run, then top to the Full mark on the dipstick. Oil filter GM91639 (TP-6904 p.11).",
   "sparkPlug": "4 plugs, 13/16 in. socket. 24RCL/24RCLA (KG2204): Kohler GM92785, M14 x 1.25. 30RCL/30RCLA/38RCLB/38RCLC (KG2204T): Kohler GM100158 (TP-6901 p.61; TP-6904 p.25). Replace every 3 years or 500 hours.",
   "plugGap": "24RCL/24RCLA: 0.9-1.0 mm (0.036-0.040 in.). 30RCL/30RCLA/38RCLB/38RCLC: 0.7-0.8 mm - TP-6907 p.29 and TP-6902 p.23 print 0.028-0.031 in.; TP-6905 p.72 and TP-6901 p.62 print 0.028-0.030 in. Gap with a wire gauge before installing.",
   "valveClearance": "No adjustment - KG2204/KG2204T use hydraulic valve lifters (TP-6902 p.101, p.110); the TP-6902 repair spec table lists no lash setting.",
   "compression": "Standard 1379 kPa (200 psi), limit 1241 kPa (180 psi). Test warm (coolant 80°C/176°F or more), all plugs out, coil pack unplugged, throttle opened fully with the diagnostic software, crank at 250 rpm or more on a fully charged battery. If low, add a little oil: pressure rises = rings/bore; stays low = valves or head gasket (TP-6902 p.23, p.29).",
   "torque": "Spark plugs: 24RCL/A 18 Nm (13.3 ft-lb); 30/38 kW 25 Nm (18.4 ft-lb) - TP-6905/TP-6907 then say add 1/4 turn with a ratchet, TP-6901 p.47 gives the torque only. Oil filter: hand tight + 3/4 turn, 25 Nm (18.4 ft-lb). Oil pan drain plug 20-25 Nm (14.8-18.4 ft-lb). Oil cooler adapter nut 40 Nm (29.5 ft-lb) (TP-6901 p.44). Cylinder head (new bolts, oiled, 3 steps in sequence): M12 x10 88-98 Nm (64.9-72.3 ft-lb), M8 x3 19-25 Nm (14.0-18.4 ft-lb) (TP-6902 p.106). Drive belt deflection at 98 N (22 lb): new 5-7 mm (0.20-0.28 in.), used 7-8 mm (0.28-0.31 in.) (TP-6901 p.50).",
   "battery": "One 12 V BCI group 24, minimum 630 CCA at 0°F (-18°C), negative ground (TP-6906 p.12; TP-7202 p.16, p.35). Optional Kohler battery kit GM89020-KP1 (12 V, 650 CCA wet) (TP-6908 p.49). RDC2 built-in charger: 13.4 V ±2%, 2.5 A max, needs 120 VAC utility feed (TP-6905 p.38). Battery charging alternator 14 V / 90 A.",
   "airFilter": "Dry element, Kohler GM90281 (TP-6908 p.6-7). Check and clean quarterly or every 20 h; replace every 3 years or 400 h; more often in dust. Clean only by tapping on a flat surface - no liquid, no compressed air (TP-6907 p.23, p.27).",
   "fuelPressure": "5-11 in. WC (1.2-2.7 kPa) at the fuel solenoid valve port (1/8-27 NPT), generator running at rated load, NG and LPG (TP-6907 p.99; spec sheets). Secondary (engine) regulator max inlet 2.7 kPa / 6 oz per sq. in. / 11 in. WC (TP-6907 p.98). Regulator outlet: NG 1-3 in. WC pressure, LPG 1-4 in. WC vacuum (TP-6903 p.48). Do not adjust the IEPR regulator or mixer.",
   "exercise": "Factory default Unloaded Cycle, weekly, 20 min: about 10 min reduced speed (idle 1350 rpm default), 3 min full speed with system diagnostics, 5 min reduced-speed cooldown, plus ramps. Other modes: Unloaded Full Speed (20 min) and Loaded Full Speed (RXT only - building loses power up to 10 s at each transfer). Weekly or every other week. Controller must be in AUTO (TP-6905 p.21, p.23-26)."
  },
