  "installNotes": [
   "Outdoor install only. At least 0.9 m (3 ft) from any building or structure and near the gas service; keep 2.4 m (8 ft) clear of combustibles beyond the exhaust end; point exhaust away from the building and openings (TP-6809 p.15). Operation manual: 0.9 m (3 ft) clearance all sides and no windows, vents or openings within 1.5 m (5 ft) of the exhaust outlet (TP-6810 p.15).",
   "Pad: 76 mm (3 in.) gravel under a 100 mm (4 in.) concrete pad with anchor bolts and stub-ups; remove the shipping bracket under the engine (TP-6809 p.15).",
   "Approx. weights: 38RCL 726 kg (1600 lb), 48RCL 862 kg (1900 lb), 48RCLA 830 kg (1830 lb), 60RCL 890 kg (1960 lb). Lift with bars through the four skid holes and a spreader bar, never by the engine/alternator eyes or the enclosure (TP-6809 p.12-13).",
   "Fuel: 1 in. NPT inlet; Schedule 40 black iron; flexible section at least 152 mm (6 in.); pipe stubbed within 254 mm (10 in.) of the inlet. Size pipe from the primary regulator, adding 2.4 m (8 ft) per 90 degree elbow; table assumes 0.5 psi (13.8 in. WC) or less with 0.5 in. WC drop (TP-6809 p.31-32).",
   "Max fuel flow at full load (TP-6809 p.31): 38RCL NG 545 cfh / LP 224 cfh; 48RCL NG 699 / LP 283; 48RCLA NG 757 / LP 283; 60RCL NG 790 / LP 330 cfh. Example pipe size for NG at 6.1 m (20 ft): 38RCL 1-1/4 in., 48RCL/48RCLA/60RCL 1-1/4 in.; at 30.5 m (100 ft): 38RCL 1-1/2 in., others 2 in.",
   "Fuel conversion: LP = remove lead 73A from the fuel valve, plug in 73B, join lead 65 to N3 (ground); NG = disconnect 65 from N3, remove 73B, connect 73A. Then set Fuel Type on the RDC2 (Genset System menu, firmware 4.5+) and order a new nameplate. Do not adjust the IEPR or mixer (TP-6809 p.33; TP-6811 p.88).",
   "Battery: BCI group 24, 12 V, 630 CCA at 0 F. Connect red to +, black to -. Battery connection triggers the date/time/exercise prompts (TP-6809 p.30).",
   "120 VAC: provide a utility circuit backed by the generator for the built-in charger (50 W, 0.42 A) and accessories: block heater 1500 W / 12.5 A at 120 V, battery heater 80 W / 0.7 A (TP-6809 p.19-20).",
   "ATS: Model RXT talks over RBUS (terminals A, B, PWR, COM); engine start terminals 3 and 4 are NOT used with RXT. Other ATS (e.g., Model RDT): wire the ATS engine-start contacts to 3 and 4 (close to run) (TP-6809 p.22-23).",
   "RBUS cable: 20 AWG shielded twisted pair (Belden 9402 indoor, 1075A outdoor/buried); max run 61 m (200 ft) with 1 module, 31 m (100 ft) with 2, 21 m (67 ft) with 3; PWR/COM can use 14 AWG (152/152/122 m) or 12 AWG (152 m). Ground shields at the generator only; up to 3 RBUS devices (one RXT, one PIM, one load management device) (TP-6809 p.25; TP-6811 p.29).",
   "SB-813: de-energize the RDC2 (open the 120 VAC breaker and remove the battery negative, unplug the SiteTech USB) before landing RBUS wires; shorting the 13 VDC PWR to A or B kills the controller (Accy PwrOver then ATS ComError in the log).",
   "Load leads go from the set's line breaker to the ATS emergency lugs; neutral ships bonded to ground at the alternator and may be lifted if the site needs an ungrounded neutral at the generator (TP-6809 p.20-21).",
   "OnCue Plus is included: always-on internet, Cat 5e cable to the customer router (use a repeater/switch over 100 m / 328 ft), UPS recommended (TP-6809 p.21, p.36).",
   "Cooling fill: 50/50 long-life coolant, run with cap off until the upper hose is hot, cool, top up to just below the overflow tube; fill before energizing a block heater (TP-6809 p.34).",
   "Startup: set date/time/exercise, press RUN, check output with a DVM and calibrate if needed (Generator Metering > Volts > Select, match the meter), OFF, then AUTO; lock the enclosure (TP-6809 p.35-36; TP-6811 p.47).",
   "Controller replacement setup: enter genset model (38RCL/48RCL/48RCLA/60RCL) and serial number (SiteTech), system voltage, frequency, phase connection, fuel type; update firmware; calibrate voltage; reset the OnCue password (TP-6811 p.42-46)."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Older-family service manual note: never change the ECM Model setting in SiteTech; picking the genset model auto-selects the engine and ECM (TP-6811 p.29).",
   "SB-777 (48RCLA and 60RCL with 5.7 L, serials SGM32GMNC to SGM32M7HN, built June 9 2016 - March 13 2018): rough running or controller resets from EMI caused by distributor cap/rotor. Cap with a V# mark is OK; a rotor with a blue contact cover and uncoated brass contact gets replaced with cap GM87989 and rotor GM87990. SB-777 closed SB-767 and its shield kit GM104032-S1.",
   "SB-767/SB-777: a controller found 'reset' (Not In Auto, exercise not scheduled, date/time not set) is first a battery problem - supply to the controller must stay at 9 V or more while cranking. Only suspect EMI if the log has no battery warnings.",
   "SB-752: RDC2 controllers with a green circuit board built before Sept 15 2014 on 38/48RCL improve battery charging with diode harness kit GM95500 (TT-1647). Red or blue boards do not need it; the build date is on the bar code label on the back of the controller.",
   "Oil filter leak on the 5.7 L: SB-807 says oil filter GM101269 (older design shipped before 4/1/2021) can leak; tightening does not fix it - replace it with the new design (wrench flats on the bottom).",
   "Fuel valve quick test: remove the + lead, apply 12 VDC, listen for a click (TP-6811 p.87).",
   "Low/no voltage quick split: shine a flashlight on the exposed photo transistor with the set running at no load - output should go high. If it does, the alternator side is OK and the fault is in wiring, controller or LED optic board (TP-6811 p.78-79).",
   "Engine speed adjust: rpm = (Hz x 30) + (setting - 50). Speed gains live in the ECM and cannot be adjusted (TP-6811 p.83).",
   "After a battery disconnect the controller prompts for date, time and exerciser; set them or the set shows Chk DateTime and Exer Not Sch and will not exercise (TP-6810 p.32).",
   "ECM codes: E-Controls diagnostic kit GM42033 reads/clears DTCs on PSI GM 4.3/5.0/5.7 L engines; ECM manual TP-6724 is included in the kit (SB-750).",
   "TP-6724 is a generic PSI certified-stationary ECM manual; it never names Kohler or the RCL, so confirm the ECM/IEPR on the unit before relying on pinouts. Its master DTC chart (p.88-91) also lists many codes that do not apply to these gaseous sets (injectors, boost, gasoline).",
   "CONFLICT: GM base-engine manuals give a 0.060 in. plug gap (TP-6104 p.11; TP-6103 p.14) - those are for the gasoline vehicle engine. Use the generator manuals' 0.035 in. (0.9 mm) (TP-6810 p.58; TP-6101 p.21)."
  ],
