  "installNotes": [
   "Clearances: per the dimension drawing (ADV8954 for 48RCLB/60RCLA, ADV9760 for 48RCLC/60RCLB) and local code; clear combustibles around the set and beyond the exhaust outlet (TP-7101 p.15; TP-7203 p.19-20).",
   "Approx. weights: 48RCLB / 48RCLC 767 kg (1690 lb); 60RCLA / 60RCLB 859 kg (1894 lb). Lift with bars through the skid holes and a spreader bar (TP-7101 p.12; TP-7203 p.17).",
   "Fuel pipe sizing (TP-7101 p.31): max flow 48RCLB NG 909.9 cfh (25.8 m3/h), LPG 498.2 cfh; 60RCLA NG 1053 cfh (29.8 m3/h), LPG 564.1 cfh. Example NG pipe: 48RCLB 1-1/4 in. to 6.1 m (20 ft), 2 in. at 18.3-45.7 m (60-150 ft); 60RCLA 1-1/2 in. at 6.1 m (20 ft), 2 in. at 12.2-30.5 m (40-100 ft). Table assumes 0.5 psi (13.8 in. WC) or less with a 0.5 in. WC drop; add 2.4 m (8 ft) per 90 degree elbow.",
   "Fuel connection: 1 in. NPT with a flexible section (do not bend it to make up misalignment); pipe stubbed within 254 mm (10 in.); leak test with soapy water; with the engine running confirm supply pressure with a manometer at the fuel valve (TP-7203 p.37).",
   "48RCLB/60RCLA conversion: LPG = connect lead 49 to lead N17 (ground) and set Fuel Type LPG in Genset System; NG = disconnect 49 from N17 and set NG. Leads are near the fuel valves, may be taped to the harness (TP-7101 p.33; TP-7103 p.95-96).",
   "48RCLC/60RCLB conversion NG to LPG (TP-7203 p.40): remove 70T/70H and N16 from FV1 and connect 70R/70G and N28; remove 70T and 77 from FV2 and connect 78 and 70R; connect N17 to 49; set Fuel Type LPG. LPG to NG is the reverse (disconnect N17 from 49; FV1 back to 70T/70H and N16; FV2 back to 70T and 77; set NG). Not for auto dual-fuel units. Tape unused leads.",
   "Dual fuel changeover kit (48RCLC/60RCLB, TT-1803): a pressure switch on the NG supply energizes a relay that closes NG and opens LP; reset box light is on while on LP. It returns to NG when LP runs out, the set stops and restarts, or the reset switch is turned clockwise and held (TP-7102 p.64; TP-7203 p.38-39).",
   "Do not adjust the DEPR or the air/fuel mixer (emission parts) (TP-7103 p.92).",
   "Battery: BCI group 24, 12 V, 630 CCA at 0 F (TP-7101 p.30; TP-7203 p.34).",
   "120 VAC circuit (utility, backed by the generator) for the charger (50 W / 0.42 A), block heater 1500 W (12.5 A at 120 V, 6.3 A at 240 V), battery heater 80 W / 0.7 A (TP-7101 p.19; TP-7203 p.24). 48RCLC/60RCLB also feed a GFCI outlet from it (TP-7203 p.26).",
   "RBUS (RXT, APM, PIM, load management): 20 AWG Belden 9402 (indoor) or 1075A (outdoor/buried) for A/B - max 46 m (150 ft) with 1 module, 15 m (50 ft) with 2, 5 m (17 ft) with 3; do not use 20 AWG for PWR/COM with 4 modules; 14 AWG PWR/COM 137 m (450 ft) for 1-2 modules (TP-7101 p.25; TP-7203 p.30). These are shorter than the older RCL table.",
   "SB-813: power down the RDC2 (open the 120 VAC breaker, remove battery negative, unplug SiteTech USB) before landing RBUS wires.",
   "Startup: set language, date, time, exercise; RUN, check output voltage, calibrate if needed; OFF then AUTO; OnCue Plus included (TP-7203 p.46-47; TP-7102 p.26).",
   "Controller replacement: genset model (48RCLB or 60RCLA per TP-7103), serial, voltage/frequency/phase, fuel type; firmware 1.3.1+ on RDC2.4 blue board; calibrate voltage; reset OnCue password (TP-7103 p.37-49)."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Do not use the older RCL fuel conversion leads (73A/73B/65) on these units - KG6208 sets use lead 49 to N17, and the RCLC/60RCLB also need FV1/FV2 lead swaps (TP-7101 p.33; TP-7203 p.40).",
   "Break-in oil: run at least 40 h, then change at the normal 150 h service (TP-7102 p.71; TP-7095 p.36).",
   "SB-807: oil filter GM101269 made before 4/1/2021 can leak on 6.2 L engines; replace it with the new design (wrench flats on the bottom) - tightening will not fix it.",
   "ECM codes: E-Controls kit GM42033 plus 6.2 L harness GM105612 (or update kit GM106069-S) reads/clears active and historic DTCs, records plots and runs ignition cut-out tests; the 4G ECM label says '4G' (SB-750).",
   "Fault names differ between the service manual (TP-7103) and the newer operation manual (TP-7102), e.g. Frequency High Shutdwn vs Frequency Over Shutdown; both are listed here.",
   "Battery CrLo Warning (below 11 V for 10 s) and Oil Temperature High Warning appear only in TP-7102 (newer firmware).",
   "Spark plug gap is 0.76 mm (0.030 in.) - not the 0.9 mm (0.035 in.) used on the older GM-engine RCL.",
   "Compression check: lowest cylinder must be at least 70% of the highest; standard 200 psi, limit 180 psi warm with throttle held open (TP-7096 p.31-32).",
   "Fuel pressure NG 7-11 in. / LP 5-11 in. at rated load at the downstream solenoid port; most hunting and surging is fuel pressure, air cleaner or blocked airflow (TP-7103 p.89, p.94).",
   "TP-7097 does not list a DEPR outlet pressure or sensor resistance tables; it only gives DTC thresholds and tree values. On residential RDC2 sets one of the two coolant temperature sensors shown is not used (TP-7097 p.17, p.23). Turbo-only codes (234-299, 1325 knock, wastegate) do not apply to the naturally aspirated KG6208."
  ],
