  "engine": "Kohler CH980, 4-cycle air-cooled twin, 999 cc (61 cu. in.), bore x stroke 90 x 78.5 mm, compression ratio 8.8:1, full-pressure lubrication, capacitor-discharge ignition with digital spark advance (DSAI), electronic governor (stepper motor + magnetic pickup); 3600 rpm at 60 Hz, 3000 rpm at 50 Hz (TP-6519 p.13, p.61)",
  "fuel": "Natural gas or LP vapor, field-convertible. Ships set for natural gas with the loose LP orifice tied near the fuel line. LP = orifice in the hose fitting at the regulator + DSAI leads 65 and N5 disconnected. NG = orifice removed + DSAI leads connected (TP-6519 p.70-71; TP-6514 p.26-27; TP-6792 p.19-20)",
  "years": "About 2009-2013 production (SB-695 6/09, SB-696 12/09, TP-6616 7/09; install manual TP-6514 covers units built before Oct 2011, TP-6792 after Oct 2011). TP-6515 4/26 lists 17/18RES and 18TRES as no longer available.",
