  "specs": {
   "oil": "Synthetic 5W-30, API service class SG, SH or SJ (TP-6519 p.19; TP-6515 p.40). Install manuals: synthetic, API SG or higher (TP-6514 p.13; TP-6792 p.13). The CH940-CH1000 engine manual recommends Kohler PRO 10W-50 or other oils by temperature (ES-652 p.4) - follow the generator manuals.",
   "oilCapacity": "Approx. 2.8 L (3.0 qt.) with filter; fill to the F mark on the dipstick, run 1 minute, stop, wait 1 minute, top up to F (TP-6519 p.13, p.20; TP-6515 p.41). CONFLICT: engine manual lists refill capacity 1.9-2.6 L (2.0-2.7 U.S. qt.) for CH940-CH1000 (ES-652 p.14) - go by the dipstick.",
   "sparkPlug": "Part number not given in the text docs (see parts catalog TP-6518). Engine manual plug data: 14 mm thread, 19.1 mm (3/4 in.) reach, 15.9 mm (5/8 in.) hex (ES-652 p.39).",
   "plugGap": "0.76 mm (0.030 in.) (TP-6519 p.13, p.20; TP-6515 p.43; ES-652 p.39)",
   "valveClearance": "CH980 uses hydraulic valve lifters (ES-652 p.20, p.37); the generator manuals list no valve lash setting.",
   "compression": "Engine manual (CH940-CH1000): Command twins - test warm, choke off, throttle wide open; at least 160 psi and no more than 15% difference between cylinders. Engines with automatic compression release (ACR) read low - use the cylinder leakdown test instead (ES-652 p.28).",
   "torque": "Spark plug 24.4-29.8 Nm (18-22 ft. lb.) (TP-6519 p.14, p.20; TP-6515 p.43); engine manual says 27 Nm (20 ft. lb.) (ES-652 p.39). Alternator overbolts 7 Nm (5 ft. lb. / 60 in. lb.); rotor thrubolt 53 Nm (39 ft. lb.); generator adapter screws 40 Nm (28 ft. lb.); muffler flange nuts 24 Nm (17.7 ft. lb.); oil filter 3/4 to 1 turn after gasket contact (TP-6519 p.14, p.79, p.81-82). Stepper motor bracket/carburetor nuts 7.5-9.1 Nm (66-81 in. lb.) with Loctite 242 (SB-696). Engine manual: cylinder head fasteners in 2 steps, 23.7 Nm (210 in. lb.) then 46.9 Nm (415 in. lb.); flywheel retaining screw 69.8 Nm (51 ft. lb.) (ES-652 p.15).",
   "battery": "12 V, negative ground. TP-6514 p.31: minimum 525 CCA at 0 F. CONFLICT: TP-6792 p.25: minimum 500 CCA at 0 F. Battery purchased separately; reversed battery = no start and possible circuit board damage. Controller draw 250 mA at 12 VDC (TP-6519 p.13).",
   "airFilter": "Replaceable high-density paper element, no precleaner on 17/18 kW; held by a latch under a cover with 2 knobs. Do not wash or blow out the element. Check daily or before starting (TP-6519 p.21; TP-6515 p.46). Part number: see TP-6518.",
   "fuelPressure": "NG and LP: 7-11 in. water column (1.7-2.7 kPa, 4-6 oz./in.2), measured at the secondary regulator inlet with the set running at rated load (TP-6519 p.13, p.69). Secondary regulator max inlet 11 in. WC (280 mm, 2.7 kPa) (TP-6519 p.69). Install manuals: 7-11 in. WC for 17/18 kW on both fuels (TP-6514 p.22; TP-6792 p.15).",
   "exercise": "Run without load once a week for 20 minutes (TP-6515 p.24). The manuals give no exercise setting on the ADC-RES: exercise from an ATS with an exercise option, or run it with an operator present.",
   "oilPressure": "172-241 kPa (25-35 psi) (TP-6519 p.13). Check with a gauge in place of the LOP switch before condemning the switch (TP-6519 p.68).",
   "magPickup": "Air gap 0.5 mm (0.020 in.), measured at 3-4 places on ring gear teeth; 1.75 VAC minimum during cranking; resistance 1.3-1.9 kOhm across QCON1-QCON2 (TP-6519 p.61, p.63-64).",
   "alternator": "Rotor 5.2 ohms cold. Stator cold (single-phase): leads 1-2, 3-4 0.06 ohm; 11-44 0.13 ohm; 55-66 0.60 ohm. 18TRES: 1-4, 2-5, 3-6, 7-10, 8-11, 9-12 0.10 ohm; 55-66 0.19 ohm. Brushes new 19.05 mm (0.75 in.), resistance through brushes 0.1-0.2 ohm (TP-6519 p.14, p.54)."
  },
