  "engine": "GM 1.6L OHC inline 4-cylinder, water-cooled, emission-certified PSI stationary engine with Integrated Electronic Pressure Regulator (IEPR = ECM + electronic fuel pressure regulator) and air/fuel mixer (NOT a Kohler Command engine). 15 kW 1800 rpm, 30 kW 3600 rpm (60 Hz). Same base engine data as RES/RYG in TP-6198 p.13. Fuel/ECM diagnostic manual TP-6724 (PSI certified stationary, GM/PSI 1.6-8.8 L); base engine manual TP-6362.",
  "fuel": "Natural gas or LP vapor through the IEPR (emission device - do NOT adjust the IEPR or mixer). Fuel type set by leads at the fuel solenoid valve: NG = lead 73A on the valve, 73B off, lead 65 off N3; LP = 73B on the valve, 73A off, lead 65 to N3 (ground) (TP-6725 p.22; TP-6727 p.32). Supply 7-11 in. WC, 3/4 NPT inlet. UL 2200 units have two fuel solenoid valves.",
  "years": "c. 2010-2013 (doc dates: SB-703 6/10, TP-6725/6726/6727/6728 10/11, TP-6729 12/11, spec sheets G4-166 to G4-169 2/13)",
