  "installNotes": [
   "Enclosed units outdoors only: 0.9 m (3 ft) from buildings; 2.4 m (8 ft) clear beyond the exhaust end; exhaust end not toward building openings (TP-6725 p.17; TP-6727 p.26). Operation manual: 1.5 m (5 ft) all sides, no openings within 5 ft of exhaust outlet (TP-6726 p.13).",
   "Pad 76 mm (3 in.) gravel + 100 mm (4 in.) concrete. Enclosed approx. 500 kg (1100 lb); open REYG approx. 325 kg (720 lb). Lift through skid holes, not lifting eyes (TP-6725 p.16-17; TP-6727 p.27).",
   "Open 15/30REYG: indoors with piped exhaust; 457 mm (18 in.) clearance; max backpressure 10.2 kPa (3.0 in. Hg); exhaust pipe 914 mm (36 in.) from combustibles; silencer backpressure as RYG (TP-6727 p.21-22, p.26).",
   "Fuel: 3/4 NPT inlet; 7-11 in. WC; flex section min 152 mm (6 in.); shutoff within 254 mm (10 in.); same pipe-size table as RES (20 ft 3/4 / 1-1/4 in. up to 200 ft 1-1/4 / 2 in.; add 8 ft per 90° elbow) (TP-6725 p.11, p.21; TP-6727 p.30).",
   "Gas flow: TP-6725 p.20 (RESA) 15 kW 200,000, 30 kW 450,000 Btu/hr; TP-6727 p.30 (REYG) 15 kW 205,000 NG / 212,500 LP, 30 kW 548,000 NG / 547,500 LP Btu/hr. Full-load NG 200 cfh (15) / 450 cfh (30); LP 85 / 180 cfh.",
   "IEPR and air/fuel mixer are calibrated emission devices - do not adjust them (TP-6725 p.12, p.22). There is no mixture/O2-sensor adjustment procedure for these models.",
   "Fuel conversion at the fuel solenoid valve: LP = disconnect 73A, connect 73B to valve, connect lead 65 to N3 (ground). NG = disconnect 65 from N3, disconnect 73B, connect 73A to valve (TP-6725 p.22; TP-6727 p.32).",
   "Electrical: breaker max 125% rated current within 7.6 m (25 ft); wire for 115% current; DC and AC in separate conduit; neutral ships bonded. 15/30RESA single-phase 120/240 V 60 Hz only, not reconnectable (TP-6725 p.12-14). Units with a customer connection box: make all AC connections at TB2 (GND and L0 there) and DC/engine start/relay connections at TB1 - do not remove the end panel (TP-6725 p.18-19).",
   "Engine start leads 3 and 4 (pigtail harness or TB1); aux fault leads 30 and N. Optional run/common fault relays: lead 88 CF NO (TB1-11), 89 CF common (TB1-12), 90 CF NC (TB1-13), 91 run NO (TB1-14), 92 run common (TB1-15), 93 run NC (TB1-16); 16 ga or larger (TP-6725 p.25).",
   "Battery 525 CCA; charger float/equalize 3 A+; 120 VAC receptacle backed up by the generator; block heater below 16°C (60°F), fill coolant first (TP-6725 p.14, p.19-20, p.26).",
   "ADC 2100 firmware 3.25 or later is REQUIRED (Ec11/Ec12 need it); version shows when entering setup (TP-6725 p.27; TP-6727 p.37).",
   "Setup mode: hold Select, switch to RUN (engine will not start), wait ~5 s for firmware version, press DOWN then UP three times, release Select. Uu -> Uc -> Ec -> Adnc (UP enters Ed -> Bt -> Cn) -> SAVE; arrow at SAVE flashes YES or no and exits; then OFF/RESET. Auto-exits without saving after ~1 min (TP-6725 p.29-30).",
   "15/30RESA settings: Uu01 (1-ph 3-wire 60 Hz 120/240), Uc01, Ec11 = 30RESA / Ec12 = 15RESA, Ed01, Bt12, Cn00 (factory, no CAN, 48-h power down) / Cn01 (J1939, no power down) / Cn06 (J1939 + 1-h power down), CA01 CANbus address (shown only on ECM engines) (TP-6725 p.28).",
   "15/30REYG settings: Uu01 120/240 1-ph; Uu04 277/480 wye; Uu10 120/240 delta or 139/240 wye; Uu11 120/208 wye; Uu16 127/220 wye (all 60 Hz); Uc01; Ec11 = 30REYG / Ec12 = 15REYG; Ed01; Bt12; Cn00/Cn01/Cn06; CA01 (TP-6727 p.38). TP-6198 p.44 lists only Ec03/Ec06 (RES/RYG) - use Ec11/Ec12 for RESA/REYG.",
   "Voltage adjust (engine running): RUN, hold Select ~5 s until version, DOWN then UP x3; 1P coarse (5 V/step at 85-132 VAC, 7 V/step at 180-251 VAC) / fine (0.5-0.7 V), 2P gain, 3P volts/Hz 0.5% per step; SAVE. Cut-in 57.5 Hz fixed (TP-6725 p.31-33; TP-6198 p.41-43, p.55-56).",
   "Controller replacement: reconfigure Uu, Uc, Ec, Ed, Bt, Cn (and CA) and recheck voltage (TP-6198 p.39-40; TP-6725 p.28).",
   "REYG 3-phase reconnection: 12-lead only, reset Uu, order decal 246242; do not change frequency (60 to 50 Hz) in the field (TP-6727 p.45-46).",
   "Oil makeup kit (30 kW): adds 2 qt with glass sight gauge; check sight gauge height at install (TP-6725 p.26)."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "30RESA/30REYG on LP with spec numbers starting GM69190 may start hard: install air intake resonator kit GM75873 and reflash the ECM (tool GM42033, file from Kohler Generator Field Service by serial number) per TT-1549. Spec GM74628 units have it from the factory (SB-703).",
   "Do not touch the IEPR or mixer adjustments - they are emission-calibrated; fuel problems are diagnosed with pressure checks (7-11 in. WC) and the PSI diagnostic tool per TP-6724 (TP-6725 p.12).",
   "Replacement ADC 2100 must run firmware 3.25+ and be set to Ec11 (30 kW) or Ec12 (15 kW) - the older Ec03/Ec06 values in TP-6198 are for RES/RYG only (TP-6725 p.27-28).",
   "SCF0 for 1-2 s at switch-on is normal; steady SCF0 = call Generator Field Service before replacing the controller (SB-725).",
   "Pull the last 20 faults with run hours before clearing: hold Select + RUN, then both arrows until F__1 (TP-6726 p.29; SB-716).",
   "Display dark in AUTO: normal 48-h (Cn00) or 1-h (Cn06) power-down; remote start or RUN wakes it (TP-6726 p.17).",
   "Fuses: F1 aux winding 10 A (358337), F2 RIB 10 A (223316), F3 controller 10 A (223316) at the junction box; four more engine fuses in the engine fuse box (TP-6726 p.29).",
   "Check config before replacing the controller, and replace the SCR module before the controller on voltage complaints (TP-6198 p.25, p.29).",
   "Oil change on these models is 150 hr / 3 months per the 2011 operation manuals; the 2015 service manual schedule prints 200 hr (TP-6726 p.20; TP-6198 p.21).",
   "Service parts: maintenance kit GM62348-SKP1-QS, air element GM16944, oil filter GM28351, plug GM35826, belt GM28353 (15 kW) / GM28352 (30 kW) (TP-6198 p.11)."
  ],
