  "installNotes": [
   "Only for Kohler generators with RDC2 or DC2. The RXT has no engine-start terminals; generator terminals 3 and 4 are not used (TP-7193 p.30-33).",
   "Match the nameplate voltage, frequency and phase to both sources; a mismatched install can cause non-warrantable damage (TP-7193 p.23).",
   "Run AC power in separate conduit from RBUS/control wiring (TP-7193 p.28).",
   "Ground the shield at the generator end only; tie shields together between modules; leave the last device's shield open (TP-7193 p.33; TP-7199 p.52).",
   "Units from 2022 on may have a single-row P10 connector rated for two 16 AWG wires: splice PWR and COM (e.g. Wago 221-413) on middle devices; A/B need no splice (TP-7239 p.1-2).",
   "Jan-Mar 2012 RXTs: the green T-block RBUS labels were reversed; wire per the interface board labels (TP-7199 p.51).",
   "One RXT, one PIM and one load-management device (LCM, load shed kit OR combined board) per generator; the combined board counts as two RBUS devices (TP-7199 p.53).",
   "Service-entrance models ship with the neutral-to-ground bonding jumper installed; remove it for non-SE use (TP-7193 p.29).",
   "100 A load-center units take Square D QO/QOA/QOC/QOP/QOT, 20 A max non-CTL tandem: 12-space (12 tandem max) or 16-space (8 tandem max); breaker ratings must match the main panel; cover unused spaces (TP-7193 p.28).",
   "Combined board: CT on the emergency leads inside the ATS with leads crossing in opposite directions; CT leads to TB1; 120 VAC to TB2 AC1/N from a generator-backed, non-shed circuit; P11 jumper across 2-3 enables load management; single-phase RDC2/DC2 firmware 5.04+ only; never add a load shed kit or LCM unless the combined board is disabled (TP-7193 p.35-41).",
   "If a 14RESA/20RESA was converted to LP, change fuel type/Genset Power Rating in the controller or SiteTech or load shed will use the NG rating (TP-7193 p.49).",
   "Check manual operation before energizing; never operate by hand with power on; leave the switch in Normal (TP-7193 p.24).",
   "Let the unit warm to room temperature 24 h before unpacking; clean with vacuum or dry cloth, never compressed air (TP-7193 p.21).",
   "SE models: optional 15 or 20 A single-pole auxiliary breaker on the load side for the generator battery charger (TP-7193 p.43, p.52).",
   "Test right after install and monthly; register startup within 60 days (TP-7193 p.44)."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Interface board LEDs - 1-ph standard board: LED1 normal available, LED2 emergency available, LED3 board power, LED4 load control relay, LED5 RBUS comm. 3-ph board: LED1 load control relay, LED2 emergency available, LED3 normal available, LED4 power, LED5 RBUS. Combined board: LED5 = power (TP-7199 p.71-72).",
   "Optional status panel: Utility Available (green) on = utility OK; Utility Connected (green) on = ATS in Normal; Generator Available (red) on = set running and making power; Generator Connected (red) on = ATS in Emergency. Load LEDs (combined panel only): red = shed, green = added, flashing red = disconnected for test (TP-7199 p.81).",
   "GM84662-KP1-QS panel fits the standard board only; GM84662-KP2-QS fits the combined board only (different ribbon connectors), even if load management is disabled (TP-7199 p.81).",
   "Load shed relay test: generator in RUN (not AUTO) and ATS NOT transferred; press TEST to step through relays; test ends after 15 min, or hold TEST 5 s, or press OFF/AUTO (TP-7193 p.48).",
   "SiteTech calls Normal 'Source 1' and Emergency 'Source 2'. Changing genset system voltage also changes Source 1 voltage, but not the other way round (TP-7199 p.44).",
   "Calibrate voltage on the RDC2: ATS Status > Normal Voltage > Select, arrow to match your meter, Select to save; repeat for Emergency with the set running. SiteTech factor: new = (meter / displayed) x old factor (TP-7199 p.74-76).",
   "Operation sequence test: each delay must be within 10% of its setting, otherwise the manual calls for replacing the controller assembly (TP-7199 p.80).",
   "A burned solenoid almost always means the mechanism was binding or something held the coil on; find that before replacing the coil (TP-7199 p.64).",
   "OnCue Plus shows a Load Shed tab when the controller recognizes the load-management device (TP-7199 p.56).",
   "A Model RDT is not an RBUS device (TP-7199 p.56)."
  ],
