  "installNotes": [
   "Engine start leads go to P2-3 and P2-4 on the GREEN 6-pin connector on the main logic board - not the similar black P9 on the accessory board (TP-7192 p.28).",
   "Neutral connection is required for the ATS to operate (TP-7192 p.22).",
   "Normal source to NA/NB, generator to EA/EB, load to LA/LB (factory-wired on load-center models) (TP-7192 p.22).",
   "SE models ship with the neutral-to-ground bonding jumper connected; disconnect it for non-SE use. Apply thread sealant if SE conduit-hub screws are removed (TP-7192 p.22).",
   "Load center: 100B 16 spaces (8 tandem max), 200B 24 (12), 200BSE 42 (10); Square D QO/QOA/QOC/QOP/QOT, 20 A max non-CTL; match main-panel ratings (TP-7192 p.21).",
   "SE: 15 A battery-charger breaker CB1 standard (to TB1); optional carb/engine heater CB2 15 A, enclosure heater CB3; SPD remote contact 2 A @ 250 VAC (TP-7192 p.33-34).",
   "Set the P5 frequency jumper for 50 or 60 Hz (TP-7192 p.30).",
   "Accessory board is required for EAM and programmable exerciser; set DIP 3 ON for the EAM (TP-7192 p.43-48).",
   "Load shed kit (TT-1609) only with single-phase generators with RDC2/DC2, firmware 5.04+ (TP-7192 p.51).",
   "With an RDC/DC or RDC2/DC2 generator you can have two exercise schedules; if they overlap the ATS wins. If the generator runs its own unloaded exercise, clear the ATS exercise (TP-7192 p.37)."
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Fault reset = hold Exercise + Test about 3 s. Holding both 6 s resets the controller to power-up state and ERASES the exercise schedule - re-set it afterward (TP-7192 p.40).",
   "Pressing OFF on the generator during ATS cooldown causes a Failure to Acquire Emergency fault on the ATS (TP-6346 p.46).",
   "The Test button sequence skips the engine start and retransfer delays; to check real delays, pull utility and time them (each within 10% of setting) (TP-6346 p.20, 55).",
   "Accessory board rotary switches: 10 positions, position 10 is marked 0; make sure each one clicks into a detent, not between (TP-7192 p.46; TP-6346 p.70).",
   "If the generator fails during a test, the ATS immediately goes back to utility (TP-7192 p.35).",
   "If the emergency source fails and utility is not available, the controller powers down until a source returns (TP-7192 p.41)."
  ],
